#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:16 ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:89
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:18
msgid ""
"Syncthing relies on a discovery server to find peers on the internet. Anyone "
"can run a discovery server and point Syncthing installations to it. The "
"Syncthing project also maintains a global cluster for public use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:23
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:27
msgid "Enable debug output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:31
msgid "Listen on HTTP (behind an HTTPS proxy)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:35
msgid "Print the current version number and exit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:39
msgid "Enable GZIP compression of HTTP responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:43
msgid "Certificate file (default \"./cert.pem\"). Unused in --http mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:47
msgid "Key file (default \"./key.pem\"). Unused in --http mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:51
msgid "Listen address (default \":8443\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:55
msgid ""
"Prometheus compatible metrics endpoint listen address (default disabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:60
msgid "Database directory, where data is stored (default \".\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:64
msgid ""
"Interval at which the in-memory database is flushed to disk (default \"5m\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:68
msgid "Pointing Syncthing at Your Discovery Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:70
msgid ""
"By default, Syncthing uses a number of global discovery servers, signified "
"by the entry ``default`` in the list of discovery servers. To make Syncthing "
"use your own instance of stdiscosrv, open up Syncthing's web GUI. Go to "
"settings, Global Discovery Server and add stdiscosrv's host address to the "
"comma-separated list, e.g. ``https://disco.example.com:8443/``. Note that "
"stdiscosrv uses port 8443 by default. For stdiscosrv to be available over "
"the internet with a dynamic IP address, you will need a dynamic DNS service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:78
msgid ""
"Prior versions need ``/v2/`` appended to the discovery server address, e.g. "
"``https://disco.example.com:8443/v2/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:82
msgid ""
"If you wish to use *only* your own discovery server, remove the ``default`` "
"entry from the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:86
msgid "Setting Up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:91
msgid ""
"This guide assumes that you have already set up Syncthing. If you haven't "
"yet, head over to :ref:`getting-started` first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:95
msgid "Installing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:97
msgid ""
"Go to `releases <https://github.com/syncthing/discosrv/releases>`__ and "
"download the file appropriate for your operating system. Unpacking it will "
"yield a binary called ``stdiscosrv`` (or ``stdiscosrv.exe`` on Windows). "
"Start this in whatever way you are most comfortable with; double clicking "
"should work in any graphical environment. At first start, stdiscosrv will "
"generate certificate files and database in the current directory unless "
"given flags to the contrary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:105
msgid ""
"The discovery server can also be obtained through apt, the Debian/Ubuntu "
"package manager. Recent releases can be found at syncthing's `apt repository "
"<https://apt.syncthing.net/>`_. The name of the package is syncthing-"
"discosrv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:111
msgid "Configuring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:114
msgid ""
"If you are running an instance of Syncthing on the discovery server, you "
"must either add that instance to other devices using a static address or "
"bind the discovery server and Syncthing instances to different IP addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:120
msgid "Certificates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:122
msgid ""
"The discovery server provides service over HTTPS. To ensure secure "
"connections from clients there are three options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:125
msgid ""
"Use a CA-signed certificate pair for the domain name you will use for the "
"discovery server. This is like any other HTTPS website; clients will "
"authenticate the server based on its certificate and domain name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:129
msgid ""
"Use any certificate pair and let clients authenticate the server based on "
"its \"device ID\" (similar to Syncthing-to-Syncthing authentication). This "
"option can be used with the certificate automatically generated by the "
"discovery server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:134
msgid ""
"Pass the ``--http`` flag if the discovery server is behind an SSL-secured "
"reverse proxy. See below for configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:137
msgid ""
"For the first two options, the discovery server must be given the paths to "
"the certificate and key at startup. This isn't necessary with the ``http`` "
"flag::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:140
msgid ""
"$ stdiscosrv --cert=/path/to/cert.pem --key=/path/to/key.pem\n"
"Server device ID is 7DDRT7J-UICR4PM-PBIZYL3-MZOJ7X7-EX56JP6-IK6HHMW-S7EK32W-"
"G3EUPQA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:143
msgid ""
"The discovery server prints its device ID at startup. In case you are using "
"a non CA signed certificate, this device ID (fingerprint) must be given to "
"the clients in the discovery server URL::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:147
msgid ""
"https://disco.example.com:8443/?id=7DDRT7J-UICR4PM-PBIZYL3-MZOJ7X7-EX56JP6-"
"IK6HHMW-S7EK32W-G3EUPQA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:149
msgid "Otherwise, the URL will be::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:151
msgid "https://disco.example.com:8443/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:154
msgid "Reverse Proxy Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:158
msgid "A new \"X-Client-Port\" HTTP header was added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:160
msgid ""
"The discovery server can be run behind an SSL-secured reverse proxy. This "
"allows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:163
msgid ""
"Use of a subdomain name without requiring a port number added to the URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:164
msgid "Sharing an SSL certificate with multiple services on the same server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:166
msgid ""
"Note that after this configuration, if the proxy uses a valid HTTPS "
"certificate, **clients should omit the** :code:`?id=...` **parameter from "
"the discovery server URL on their configuration**. Client-side validation "
"will be done by checking the visible proxy server's HTTPS certificate. If, "
"however, the proxy uses a self-signed or somehow invalid certificate, "
"clients must still set the :code:`?id=...` parameter with the computed hash "
"of the proxy's certificate. Using such setup is discouraged and is not "
"covered in this page. Always favour using valid and widely recognised "
"certificates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:176
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:178
msgid ""
"Run the discovery server using the -http flag: :code:`stdiscosrv -http`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:179
msgid "SSL certificate/key configured for the reverse proxy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:180
msgid ""
"The \"X-Forwarded-For\" HTTP header must be passed through with the client's "
"real IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:182
msgid ""
"The \"X-Client-Port\" HTTP header should be passed through, containing the "
"client's real connection port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:183
msgid ""
"The \"X-SSL-Cert\" HTTP header must be passed through with the PEM-encoded "
"client SSL certificate. This will be present in POST requests and may be "
"empty in GET requests from clients. If you see syncthing-discosrv "
"outputting :code:`no certificates` when receiving POST requests, that's "
"because the proxy is not passing this header through."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:188
msgid ""
"The proxy must request the client SSL certificate but not require it to be "
"signed by a trusted CA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:192
msgid "Nginx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:194
msgid ""
"These lines in the configuration take care of the last four requirements "
"listed above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:197
msgid ""
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Client-Port $remote_port;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-SSL-Cert $ssl_client_cert;\n"
"ssl_verify_client optional_no_ca;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:204
msgid ""
"The following is a complete example Nginx configuration file. With this "
"setup, clients can use https://discovery.example.com as the discovery server "
"URL in the Syncthing settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:208
msgid ""
"# HTTP 1.1 support\n"
"proxy_http_version 1.1;\n"
"proxy_buffering off;\n"
"proxy_set_header Host $http_host;\n"
"proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n"
"proxy_set_header Connection $http_connection;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Client-Port $remote_port;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $http_x_forwarded_proto;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-SSL-Cert $ssl_client_cert;\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Tls-Client-Cert \"\";\n"
"proxy_set_header X-Tls-Client-Cert-Der-Base64 \"\";\n"
"upstream discovery.example.com {\n"
"    # Local IP address:port for discovery server\n"
"    server 192.0.2.1:8443;\n"
"}\n"
"server {\n"
"        server_name discovery.example.com;\n"
"        listen 80;\n"
"        access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log vhost;\n"
"        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;\n"
"}\n"
"server {\n"
"        server_name discovery.example.com;\n"
"\n"
"        listen 443 ssl http2;\n"
"        access_log /var/log/nginx/access.log vhost;\n"
"\n"
"        # Mozilla Intermediate configuration (https://wiki.mozilla.org/"
"Security/Server_Side_TLS)\n"
"        ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;\n"
"        ssl_ciphers ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:ECDHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-"
"SHA256:ECDHE-ECDSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384:ECDHE-ECDSA-"
"CHACHA20-POLY1305:ECDHE-RSA-CHACHA20-POLY1305:DHE-RSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:DHE-"
"RSA-AES256-GCM-SHA384;\n"
"        ssl_prefer_server_ciphers off;\n"
"        ssl_session_tickets off;\n"
"        ssl_session_timeout 5m;\n"
"        ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:50m;\n"
"        ssl_verify_client optional_no_ca;\n"
"\n"
"        # OCSP stapling\n"
"        ssl_stapling on;\n"
"        ssl_stapling_verify on;\n"
"\n"
"        # Certificates\n"
"        ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/certs/discovery.example.com.crt;\n"
"        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/certs/discovery.example.com.key;\n"
"\n"
"        # curl https://ssl-config.mozilla.org/ffdhe2048.txt > /path/to/"
"dhparam\n"
"        ssl_dhparam /path/to/dhparam;\n"
"\n"
"        # HSTS (ngx_http_headers_module is required) (63072000 seconds)\n"
"        add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=63072000\" always;\n"
"\n"
"        location / {\n"
"                proxy_pass http://discovery.example.com;\n"
"        }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:267
msgid ""
"An example of automating the SSL certificates and reverse-proxying the "
"Discovery Server and Syncthing using Nginx, `Let's Encrypt`_ and Docker can "
"be found here_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:275
msgid "Apache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:276
msgid "The following lines must be added to the configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:278
msgid ""
"SSLProxyEngine On\n"
"SSLVerifyClient optional_no_ca\n"
"RequestHeader set X-SSL-Cert \"%{SSL_CLIENT_CERT}s\"\n"
"RequestHeader unset X-Forwarded-Tls-Client-Cert\n"
"RequestHeader unset X-Tls-Client-Cert-Der-Base64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:286
msgid ""
"The following was observed to not be required at least under Apache httpd "
"2.4.38, as the proxy module adds the needed header by default. If you need "
"to explicitly add the following directive, make sure to issue :code:`a2enmod "
"remoteip` first. Then, add the following to your Apache httpd configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:292
msgid "RemoteIPHeader X-Forwarded-For"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:297
msgid "Caddy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:298
msgid "The following lines must be added to the Caddyfile:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:300
msgid ""
"  discovery.example.com {\n"
"    reverse_proxy 192.0.2.1:8443 {\n"
"      header_up X-Forwarded-For {http.request.remote.host}\n"
"      header_up X-Client-Port {http.request.remote.port}\n"
"      header_up X-Tls-Client-Cert-Der-Base64 {http.request.tls.client."
"certificate_der_base64}\n"
"      header_up -X-Ssl-Cert\n"
"      header_up -X-Forwarded-Tls-Client-Cert\n"
"    }\n"
"\n"
"    tls {\n"
"      client_auth {\n"
"        mode request\n"
"      }\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/stdiscosrv.rst:320
msgid ""
"For more details, see also the recommendations in the `Reverse Proxy Setup "
"<https://docs.syncthing.net/users/reverseproxy.html>`__ page. Note that that "
"page is directed at setting up a proxy for the Syncthing web UI. You should "
"do the proper path and port adjustments to proxying the discovery server and "
"your particular setup."
msgstr ""

